WEBVTT

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:37.590
Hmm, where did I put it?

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:40.860
What are you looking for?

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:45.850
This doll I got when I was a kid apparently
has a collector's premium now.

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:48.790
Not that I want to sell it, but
I thought I'd try to find it.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:55.690
<b>I ink that's a doll?</b>

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:59.330
Oh, there it is.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:01.960
Here.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.350
It's creepy!

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.810
Hey, don't be so mean.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:14.190
These used to be really
popular, you know?

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:19.730
They're called Johnny and Depp.

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:30.960
I was happy when I got one.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:33.420
I squidly don't get it.

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:38.030
Since I found it, I guess I'll
put it up in my room.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:38.880
Whaaat?!

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.080
It's time for bed.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:42.090
S-Sure.

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:52.470
I feel its eyes on me...

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.740
Turning it around just for
the night should be fine.

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:09.980
Now I can sleep.

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:20.670
Huh?

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:26.430
I'm sure I turned it
around last night.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.390
Eiko, did you turn it back?

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:31.850
No, I didn't touch it.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:40.410
I must have squimagined it.

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:23.610
Good morning.

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:28.720
- What happened, Squid Girl?!
- Is everything okay, Squiddie?

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:30.810
What's wrong, Squid Girl?

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.860
The doll! The doll!

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:36.740
Good morning.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:41.590
The doll spoke!
I knew it, it's cursed!

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:46.050
Calm down.

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:49.060
These dolls are made to do that.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:55.150
They have a built in clock and
greet you in the morning.

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:55.770
Good morning.

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:57.980
Bad taste if you ask me.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:02.330
It's supposed to also
say "Good night",

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:04.060
but maybe it's broken.

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:06.570
I guess it's just old.

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:12.240
This doll is bad for my heart.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:14.200
You'll get used to it in no time.

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:17.120
Wow, that brings back memories!

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:20.370
We used to play with
these all the time!

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:21.090
Yeah.

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:27.720
Huh? Didn't you have another
one of these?

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:29.820
You mean Johnny?

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:32.640
I thought you had that one.

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:36.600
No, I remember borrowing
yours when we played.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.850
But if we used to have both,

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:40.790
they should have been in
the same place, right?

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:41.570
True.

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:45.070
These can greet you, right?

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:48.430
Yeah, but it's broken
and can only say

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:52.020
"good morning", but
not "good night".

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:54.870
Johnny's the one who
says "good night".

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:59.080
So Depp for the morning,
and Johnny for the evening.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:01.250
Was that how it worked?

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:04.600
Maybe you do have Johnny, too.

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:08.900
Maybe... Oh, hey, Squid Girl.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:09.860
What is it?

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:12.930
You said that the doll would
be facing forward

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:15.910
even if you turned it around
at night, right?

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:16.560
Yep.

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:21.310
These dolls are sitting
on a rotating platter.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:23.320
Why do you think that is?

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:27.280
Johnny and Depp are in love.

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:30.250
At a certain time during the day,

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:32.500
their sensors react and they
turn towards each other.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:33.990
Good morning.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:33.990
Good night.

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:36.330
This means...

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:41.830
that wherever Depp is pointing,
Johnny might still be there.

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:45.150
They use infrared or something,
don't they?

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:47.280
Does that work even
when they're apart?

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:50.380
Hm... maybe this <i>is</i>
something paranormal.

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:53.300
It's infrared! I'm sure it is!

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:56.570
I guess this direction implies
it's downstairs in the storehouse.

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:07.690
Oh, it's slowly coming
back to me now.

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:31.150
I told my parents that I had

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:34.410
lost it and secretly hid Johnny
in a hard-to-find place.

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:37.780
Is this it?

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:48.480
Good ni-ni-night.

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:55.930
And thus, Johnny and Depp

00:07:55.930 --> 00:07:59.130
were reunited again after
ten years apart and are now

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:03.590
spending the rest of their
lives at a certain shrine.

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:09.300
I love you.

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:10.930
I love you.

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:20.130
I am a member of the US
laboratory in search of

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:24.560
countermeasures against extraterrestrial life.
My name is Cindy Campbell.

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:27.450
My job is to observe aliens.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:31.560
My current target is not Squid Girl,

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:34.780
but the oldest of the Aizawa
family - Aizawa Chizuru!

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:39.760
<b>Isn't that fishy?</b>

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:43.620
Nagisa, could you maybe
teach me how to surf?

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:46.550
Sure. Chizuru, would you
like to learn, too?

00:08:46.550 --> 00:08:48.710
No, no, I could never
learn how to surf.

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:51.120
Yeah right!

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:52.760
I've seen it
with my own eyes...

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:57.140
I've seen that she has
superhuman physical abilities.

00:08:57.780 --> 00:08:58.970
You don't see it?

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:08.360
Now? That's why I've decided to
study Chizuru instead.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:10.770
This time I'm serious.

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:13.110
Cindy here. Harris...

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:15.850
Are you ready?

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:18.070
Yes, Cindy.

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:24.640
With this invisibility suit, retrieving
a hair from her will be easy.

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:30.130
He really disappeared!

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:34.050
Ouch! Stop it, Harris.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:35.340
What's wrong, Martin?

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:39.090
Enema successful!

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:42.210
I have no idea where he is.

00:09:42.210 --> 00:09:44.350
Chizuru won't know
where he is either!

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:46.370
Godspeed!

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:51.850
Godspeed!

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:54.070
Just you wait.

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:55.530
Aizawa Chizuru...

00:09:58.590 --> 00:09:59.410
She's not here.

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:04.080
Uh oh.

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:05.450
Who was that?!

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:09.800
What are you doing?

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:11.670
Someone squidding bumped into me.

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:13.460
There's nobody there.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:15.640
It's true though!

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:16.810
Sheesh.

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:20.430
Sorry.

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:25.880
Th-The glass...

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:27.480
It's floating!

00:10:28.030 --> 00:10:31.440
See, I told you somebody's here!

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:39.900
What's going on?

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:44.160
C-Cindy! D-Do something!

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:47.790
You have to act! That was
definitely paranormal!

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:51.290
This thing was floating by itself!

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:55.320
Nobody saw me. Great success!

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:58.470
Now... there she is!

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:03.740
If I pull out one of her
hairs, she'll notice!

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:07.720
Wait, that's why I'm invisible.

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:11.710
Sh-She disappeared?!

00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:16.110
I thought I sensed something...

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:19.070
Maybe I imagined it.

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:30.540
I lost... Me, who graduated
top of my class from MIT...

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:33.700
No problem.

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:37.870
Leave the blood retrieval to me.

00:11:37.870 --> 00:11:42.010
Behold, an artificial fly with
cloaking technology built in.

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:44.890
But she'll hear it.

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:49.280
Try again, this fly has silencing
technology built in, too!

00:11:52.780 --> 00:11:55.020
There's nothing that I didn't
think of, after all,

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:57.610
I graduated top of my
class from MIT! Go!

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:07.570
I'm telling you, something is there!

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:11.250
I can't hear a word Clark's saying
because of these two.

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:09.710
It even picked up the broken glass!

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:13.830
Cindy, are you even listening?!

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:13.830
Something about a
fly or something?

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:16.500
No one's noticed a thing.

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:17.720
Great!

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:21.210
Keep going like that and
retrieve Chizuru's blood!

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:27.430
Even now, just thinking back
gives me the chills.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:30.390
What's he planning to
do with that fly?

00:12:30.590 --> 00:12:33.560
You should pay more attention
when we're talking!

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:37.360
Huh? Oh yeah, you're talking
about a fly, right?

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:42.480
Cloaking on.

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:48.040
Huh?

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:52.050
Oh my god!

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:54.300
Clark failed, too.

00:12:55.070 --> 00:12:58.370
You're all underestimating her!

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:00.260
I guess I'll have to go in and...

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:01.970
Leave it to me!

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:05.940
Chizuru.

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:06.720
Yes?

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:11.500
"Chizuru"

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:09.280
I'm a huge fan of yours.

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:11.510
Can I have a hair or some blood?

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:13.070
It's over...

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:14.640
All right.

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:19.060
It's not all right!

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:22.530
She didn't refuse, even though the
request came from such a creep.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:25.270
I knew she's not to be trifled with.

00:13:25.270 --> 00:13:25.900
Here you go.

00:13:28.130 --> 00:13:29.570
My head hurts.

00:13:29.940 --> 00:13:32.960
Anyway, we succeeded.

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:34.200
Let's return to our lab.

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:35.520
Yeah.

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:38.420
Hold it right there.

00:13:38.570 --> 00:13:40.250
What is this?

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:42.710
That's my artificial fly...

00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:47.130
What are you trying to achieve with
this fly and with Martin's act?

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:51.430
I suppose it's probably just another
one of your experiments.

00:13:51.940 --> 00:13:53.610
But seriously, what MIT graduate

00:13:53.610 --> 00:13:56.140
would say something like
"please give me your hair or blood"?!

00:13:57.290 --> 00:14:02.510
As long as we get our precious samples,
we don't care what the plan is.

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:05.780
Besides, why is it my sister
and not Squid Girl?

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:09.860
It better tell us everything,
or else it gets tentacled again!

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:17.750
Okay! Okay! I'll talk!

00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:26.500
W-We couldn't ignore the possibility
that Chizuru is an alien,

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:28.720
s-so we decided to investigate.

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:31.410
What? An alien? Her?

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:35.060
These people are thinking
the same thing as me.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:37.220
She's the king of aliens!

00:14:37.220 --> 00:14:38.680
We're not there yet.

00:14:38.680 --> 00:14:41.470
We're merely a little curious.

00:14:41.470 --> 00:14:43.620
We weren't being really serious.

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:46.210
I don't mind being an alien.

00:14:46.210 --> 00:14:46.780
Huh?

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:51.830
However, if proper alien conduct dictates
that I have to do some invasion work,

00:14:51.830 --> 00:14:54.780
I'll have to start by eliminating
the threat first!

00:14:56.720 --> 00:14:59.250
Pl-Please have mercy on us!

00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:04.280
Chizuru simply is invincible...

00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:17.170
We're here, Squiddie.

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:20.180
So this is the mountain you
can see from the beach.

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:29.510
I didn't realize it when I
looked at it from there,

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:32.160
but once you're here,
it's really huge!

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:35.120
All right, then let's begin our climb.

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:38.470
Climb? What are we climbing?

00:15:38.470 --> 00:15:40.120
The mountain, of course.

00:15:40.680 --> 00:15:43.290
This will be the first time
Squid Girl climbs a mountain, huh?

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:44.880
Climbs a mountain?

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:47.340
It means to go to the
top of the mountain.

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:49.250
I'm going home.

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:52.390
I don't see why you need
to go out of your way

00:15:52.390 --> 00:15:54.050
to do something that tiring.

00:15:54.690 --> 00:15:56.470
You've got to try it.

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:59.520
Once you start, you'll get into it.

00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:04.500
<b>Squids to match my mountains.</b>

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:12.700
Is it going to continue to
be uphill until the top?

00:16:13.190 --> 00:16:15.660
Well, we are climbing
a mountain, so yeah.

00:16:16.230 --> 00:16:20.100
Simply savor the kind of nature
you don't get at the ocean.

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:21.580
Nature...

00:16:22.110 --> 00:16:24.500
There are so many birds here
that I've never seen before.

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:28.710
Even our grade schooler,
Takeru, is more than fine.

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:33.300
Besides, if you're already whining
from this, you'll never ever

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:36.300
be able to achieve your dream of
conquering the surface world.

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:39.600
This is like water off a squid's back!

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:42.700
Since you had to open your mouth,
how about we race to the top?!

00:16:42.700 --> 00:16:43.810
Hey, wait!

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:49.890
I can't go on any more...

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:56.050
Why is nobody following?

00:16:56.050 --> 00:16:57.700
Because that's what happens.

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:00.160
Squid Girl, we're almost there.

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:01.230
Come on.

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:06.180
Just get over this final hump.

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:13.320
I'm tired of walking...

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:25.790
Squid Girl.

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:28.310
No cheating.

00:17:28.890 --> 00:17:31.460
Okay, fine!

00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:37.530
That squidding hurts!

00:17:38.090 --> 00:17:40.420
How dare you, you lowly squirrels!

00:17:40.420 --> 00:17:42.510
Let those squirrels be. Let's go.

00:17:43.310 --> 00:17:44.620
It's a monkey!

00:17:47.090 --> 00:17:50.900
Ow, this isn't food!

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:53.450
That looks like those mountains
you see at touristy spots.

00:17:57.810 --> 00:17:59.310
Now it's a bear!

00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:01.580
More precisely, a brown bear.

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:03.330
I don't think this is the
time to be precise!

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:04.680
Everybody, play dead!

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:12.190
Go away.

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:18.240
How often do I have to say it?
My tentacles are not food!

00:18:27.950 --> 00:18:29.970
That's a king cobra.

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:38.750
I guess it confused your tentacles
for a mongoose.

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:40.800
How's that even possible?

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:42.190
Fight, Squiddie!

00:18:42.670 --> 00:18:44.220
Oh, all right.

00:18:44.670 --> 00:18:46.750
Bring it on!

00:18:49.260 --> 00:18:51.650
Even on the mountain, I'm prey...

00:18:52.340 --> 00:18:53.650
The cobra wins.

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:56.900
Squiddie, are you okay?

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:13.790
See, we're there.

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:17.940
Finally... the top...

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:25.230
Wow, Squiddie, quickly!

00:19:27.690 --> 00:19:29.980
This is inkredible!

00:19:31.590 --> 00:19:35.570
I've never seen the ocean
from up above before.

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:37.980
I never knew it was so big.

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:40.630
Everything looks so small...

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:43.460
It makes me want to crush
everything with my feet.

00:19:43.460 --> 00:19:45.950
Looks like your invader
spirit hasn't died.

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:48.930
Yahoo!

00:19:48.930 --> 00:19:51.250
Is someone over there?

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:51.250
Yahoo!

00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:54.950
Th-There's another Chizuru
over there!

00:19:54.950 --> 00:19:57.960
That was just an echo, Squiddie.

00:19:57.960 --> 00:19:58.960
Echo?

00:19:59.310 --> 00:20:00.970
You'll understand if you yell.

00:20:01.550 --> 00:20:03.650
You have to say 'yahoo'.

00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:08.100
No way. That reminds me
of the three stooges.

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:13.340
Someone's talking about us...

00:20:16.030 --> 00:20:17.820
Yahoo!

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:20.550
Then just yell whatever you want.

00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:22.320
I'll do that.

00:20:23.210 --> 00:20:25.910
My name is Squid Girl!

00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:31.240
See, isn't it fun?

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:32.290
What's so fun about this?

00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:35.510
I am Squid Girl!

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:40.960
You are not Squid Girl!

00:20:41.350 --> 00:20:44.340
I don't think she understands
what the echo is.

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:47.960
My goodness. What's the point of
arguing with your own echo?

00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:52.400
How many times do I have
to repeat myself?

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:55.730
You are not Squid Girl, I am!

00:20:58.760 --> 00:21:02.430
Man, eating rice balls on
the summit is the best.

00:21:02.430 --> 00:21:05.420
It really feels like it was
worth the effort.

00:21:05.420 --> 00:21:06.580
Squiddie!

00:21:07.130 --> 00:21:08.660
Sanae...

00:21:10.090 --> 00:21:13.060
Why didn't you invite me?

00:21:13.060 --> 00:21:14.730
When I heard you came
to the mountains,

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:16.790
I came running right away.

00:21:17.030 --> 00:21:19.500
Good work, I guess?

00:21:20.570 --> 00:21:25.780
How come you're not tired
or sweaty at all?

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:28.930
I wanted to catch up with
you as fast as possible,

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:30.300
so I used the cable car.

00:21:30.940 --> 00:21:32.770
Cable car?

00:21:33.250 --> 00:21:34.290
This is it!

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:42.310
Wh-What was the point of walking
all the way up here?!

00:21:42.310 --> 00:21:46.660
Well, you enjoyed your
way up, didn't you?

00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:49.010
And you got to see a
bunch of rare animals!

00:21:49.010 --> 00:21:50.660
That's not the point!

00:21:51.110 --> 00:21:52.340
Here we are.

00:21:52.340 --> 00:21:55.000
I look forward to the
view from the top.

00:21:55.730 --> 00:21:58.120
No cheating! No... cheating!

00:21:58.480 --> 00:22:02.960
You are only allowed to enjoy the
view if you've walked up here.

00:22:02.960 --> 00:22:03.550
Hey.

00:22:05.520 --> 00:22:08.430
If you want to enjoy the view,
you have to walk up the mountain!

00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:09.760
You can't just make
up a rule like that!

00:23:42.440 --> 00:23:45.150
Squid Girl here. Our last episode...

00:23:45.610 --> 00:23:47.120
You feeling lucky, squid?

00:23:47.120 --> 00:23:48.610
Quite the squidicament we're in.

00:23:48.610 --> 00:23:50.440
An even worse squidicament!

00:23:50.440 --> 00:23:53.650
My Earth squid-vasion plan's
success is only a matter of time!
